# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Cactus DSL — Comprehensive Feature Showcase
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This single file demonstrates every syntactic and semantic feature of the
# Cactus DSL as defined in the openspec/specs directory and pending changes.
#
# Language identity:
#   Cactus is a declarative, data-oriented gameplay description language that
#   compiles to an engine backend. Authors describe WHAT EXISTS, WHAT REACTS TO
#   WHAT, HOW STATE CHANGES, and WHAT IS PRESENTED. The backend handles all
#   plumbing: rendering, physics integration, lifetime management, serialization.
#
# See openspec/specs/language-philosophy/spec.md for the authoritative language
# identity and design principles (predictability, total semantics, author/backend
# split, performance as backend obligation, feature evaluation criteria).
#
# Sections:
#   1.  Module declaration & imports (use, use as)
#   2.  Const block  — int, float, string, hex color (6- and 8-digit)
#   3.  Asset declarations — all six asset types
#   4.  Input declarations — button and axis
#   5.  Struct types
#   6.  Enum types
#   7.  Trait declarations — all field modifiers (let, var, persist, sync, pub)
#                           — field default values (= expr)
#   8.  Marker traits      — body-less (zero-cost tag), no fields, no alias
#   9.  Event declarations — including events with entity_id fields
#   10. Pure func declarations  — no emit, no world access, no recursion
#   11. Extern func declarations — body-less, backend-provided
#   12. Unit declarations — apply without `: disabled` (open-world traits)
#   13. Template declarations  — spawn-only blueprints
#   14. Systems — filter / exclude / order by / after / all handler phases
#       · on input                      (Input phase — no payload fields)
#       · on fixed_tick                 (Physics phase — fixed_tick.dt)
#       · on tick  [as alias]           (Update phase — tick.dt or alias.dt)
#       · on late_tick                  (Post-update phase — late_tick.dt)
#       · on spawn  / on destroy        (Entity lifecycle — no fields)
#       · on load   / on unload         (Scene lifecycle — no fields)
#       · on UserEvent  [as alias]      (Custom event — EventName.field or alias.field)
#   15. Dynamic traits — `add` / `remove` replace `enable` / `disable`
#       · add TraitName                  (bare — all defaults)
#       · add TraitName(field = val)     (named args — explicit field init)
#       · add TraitName to entity_id     (cross-entity targeting)
#       · remove TraitName               (self)
#       · remove TraitName from entity_id (cross-entity targeting)
#   16. Entity sort ordering — `order by:` clause on systems
#       · alias.field asc / desc         (primary and secondary keys)
#   17. Trait pattern matching — `match entity_id:` (double dispatch)
#       · TraitName as alias =>          (bind trait data of other entity)
#       · TraitName =>                   (marker trait — no alias)
#       · _ =>                           (optional wildcard)
#   18. Entity liveness — `exists(entity_id)` built-in
#       · entity_id is an opaque handle; may become stale when entity destroyed
#       · exists(id) → bool; guards cross-entity access; stale ops are safe no-ops
#       · match on stale id fires NO arms — including `_ =>`
#   19. Extern system — `extern system` declarations (no event handlers)
#       · stdlib-known: backend recognises trait set and auto-generates full pass
#       · user-defined: backend generates typed C++ callback scaffold
#   20. Statements — let/var, if/else, match (value + trait), emit (broadcast + targeted),
#       spawn (statement + expression), destroy (self + entity_id),
#       load, add, remove, return
#   21. Expressions — binary ops, unary, member access, function calls,
#       lambda (map), bool literals, vec2/vec3/quat constructors
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ASPIRATIONAL vs. CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION GAPS
#
# Most of this file demonstrates the INTENDED authoring pattern as specified.
# The following sections contain KNOWN GAPS where the authoring surface is not
# yet fully declarative:
#
#   · draw_rect / draw_text calls  (SceneRenderSystem, BossRenderSystem,
#     UIRenderSystem, DebugOverlaySystem, ParticleSystem)
#     → KNOWN GAP: explicit rendering calls are NOT the intended pattern.
#       The intended pattern is `extern system SpriteRenderPass` (Section 19).
#       `draw_rect` calls exist here only to illustrate system handler syntax
#       while the stdlib rendering layer is still pending.
#       Tracked by: dsl-extern-system (tasks 6.x, stdlib updates).
#
#   · play_particle_effect extern func call  (ParticleSystem)
#     → KNOWN GAP: particle effects should be driven by a trait + extern system.
#       Tracked by: dsl-declarative-audio (future change).
#
# Section 19 (extern system) shows the CORRECT declarative pattern that will
# replace all direct draw_* calls once the stdlib rendering layer is in place.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. Module declaration & imports ───────────────────────────────────────────

module showcase

use std.core                      # provides Persistent, SceneCleanup, and lifecycle events
use std.input
use std.math as math              # use ... as ALIAS form
use std.math.vec2 as v2
use std.math.vec3 as v3
use std.math.quat as quat
use std.transform.flat as tr_flat
use std.transform.volume as tr_vol
use std.render.sprites as spr
use std.render.meshes as mesh_r
use std.physics.flat as phys_flat
use std.physics.volume as phys_vol
use std.camera.flat as cam_flat
use std.camera.volume as cam_vol
use std.audio

use level2                        # referenced by load statement below
use game_over                     # referenced by load statement below

# ── 2. Const block ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Permitted literal types: integer, float, string, hex color (6-digit, 8-digit)

const:
    WINDOW_TITLE       = "DSL Showcase"
    WINDOW_WIDTH       = 1280
    WINDOW_HEIGHT      = 720
    TARGET_FPS         = 60
    GRAVITY            = 30.0
    MOVE_SPEED         = 5.0
    JUMP_FORCE         = 12.0
    MAX_HEALTH         = 100
    SCORE_PER_COIN     = 10
    PLAYER_COLOR       = #3399FF        # 6-digit RGB
    ENEMY_COLOR        = #CC3333FF      # 8-digit RGBA
    UI_BG_COLOR        = #00000080      # 8-digit RGBA (semi-transparent black)
    CLEAR_WHITE        = #FFFFFF
    SCORE_LABEL        = "Score:"
    LIVES_LABEL        = "Lives:"
    DEBUG_LABEL        = "DEBUG"

# ── 3. Asset declarations ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Six asset types: mesh, texture, sound, music, font, material.
# String path literals are exempt from the const-string rule here.
# pub makes an asset importable by other modules.

pub asset PlayerMesh:    mesh     = "models/player.glb"
pub asset PlayerTex:     texture  = "textures/player.png"
pub asset EnemyTex:      texture  = "textures/enemy.png"
    asset CoinTex:       texture  = "textures/coin.png"
    asset HitSound:      sound    = "audio/hit.wav"
    asset CoinSound:     sound    = "audio/coin.wav"
pub asset ThemeMusic:    music    = "audio/theme.ogg"
pub asset BossMusic:     music    = "audio/boss.ogg"
pub asset HudFont:       font     = "fonts/hud.ttf"
pub asset PlayerMat:     material = "materials/player.mat"

# ── 4. Input declarations ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# button: key, mouse, gamepad properties.
# axis:   negative, positive, gamepad, invert properties.

pub input Jump: button
    key     = Key.Space
    gamepad = GamepadButton.South

pub input Fire: button
    key   = Key.LeftControl
    mouse = MouseButton.Left

pub input Pause: button
    key     = Key.Escape
    gamepad = GamepadButton.Start

pub input MoveX: axis
    negative = Key.A
    positive = Key.D
    gamepad  = GamepadAxis.LeftX

pub input MoveY: axis
    negative = Key.S
    positive = Key.W
    gamepad  = GamepadAxis.LeftY
    invert   = true

# ── 5. Struct types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Value objects with typed fields; no methods or inheritance.

struct Item:
    name:  string
    price: int
    count: int

struct Bounds:
    x: float
    y: float
    w: float
    h: float

# ── 6. Enum types ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Named integer constants.

enum GameState:
    MainMenu
    Playing
    Paused
    GameOver

enum EnemyType:
    Walker
    Flyer
    Boss

enum FacingDir:
    Left
    Right

# ── 7. Trait declarations ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fields:    let (immutable after init)   var (mutable)
# Modifiers: persist (serialized to disk) sync (network-replicated)
#            pub (exported in ImportedSymbols)
# Default values: = expr on any field (used by `add` when field is omitted)

# — Primitive scalar types —
trait Health:
    let max_health: int = 100           # let: immutable, with default
    persist sync var health: int        # persist + sync + var
    pub var shield: int = 0             # pub field with default value

# — Traits with default values — bare `add TraitName` works when all fields have defaults —

trait Invincible:
    var duration: float = 1.5           # default — `add Invincible` uses this automatically

trait Stunned:
    var duration:    float = 2.0        # default duration
    var slow_factor: float = 0.5        # default movement slow

# — vec2 / float types —
trait Position2D:
    persist sync var pos:      vec2
    var velocity:              vec2

# — vec3 / quat types —
trait Transform3D:
    persist sync var pos:      vec3
    persist sync var rotation: quat
    var velocity:              vec3

# — list[T] generic type —
trait Inventory:
    var items:     list[Item]
    var gold:      int
    var max_slots: int

# — Asset opaque handle types (texture_id, mesh_id, material_id, etc.) —
trait Renderable2D:
    let texture:  texture_id            # only obtainable from an asset declaration
    var visible:  bool
    var layer:    int = 0               # default layer (background)
    var tint:     color

trait Renderable3D:
    let mesh:     mesh_id               # mesh_id opaque type
    let material: material_id           # material_id opaque type
    var visible:  bool

# — entity_id type: opaque handle; may become stale when the referenced entity is destroyed —
# Use exists(id) to test liveness. All ops on a stale handle are safe no-ops / silent no-match.
trait Parent:
    var parent_id: entity_id

trait Follower:
    var target: entity_id               # may become stale — guard with exists()
    var offset: vec3
    var speed:  float

# — color type —
trait Visual:
    var color:  color
    var width:  float
    var height: float

# — bool + enum types —
trait EnemyAI:
    var patrol_min_x:  float
    var patrol_max_x:  float
    var patrol_speed:  float
    var direction:     float = 1.0      # default: moving right
    var enemy_type:    EnemyType
    var is_aggro:      bool = false     # default: not aggressive

# — InputButton / InputAxis field types (resolved from input declarations) —
trait PlayerInput:
    let jump_action:   InputButton      # InputButton opaque type
    let move_x_action: InputAxis        # InputAxis opaque type

# — pub trait (exported in module ImportedSymbols) —
pub trait Score:
    persist var score:           int
    persist var high_score:      int
    var combo_multiplier:        int = 1    # default multiplier

# — music_id / sound_id / font_id types —
trait AudioConfig:
    let theme:   music_id
    let hit_sfx: sound_id
    let hud_fnt: font_id

# ── 8. Marker traits ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No colon, no body — zero-cost tag component; used for filter/exclude/add/remove.
# Note: `Invincible` and `Stunned` are in section 7 (they have fields).

trait Frozen                    # entity is paused/frozen — dynamically added/removed
trait PlayerOwned               # entity belongs to the player
trait Collectible               # entity can be picked up
pub trait Boss                  # pub marker: importable by other modules

# ── 9. Event declarations ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# In handlers, payload is accessed via the event name or optional alias:
#   on PlayerDamaged:      → PlayerDamaged.amount
#   on PlayerDamaged as d: → d.amount
#
# Events may carry entity_id fields — enables trait pattern matching via `match`.
# Lifecycle events (tick, fixed_tick, late_tick, spawn, destroy, input,
# load, unload) are declared as pub events in std.core and are always in scope.
# Marker events (no fields) may be declared without a body.

event PlayerJumped:
    var position: vec2
    var velocity: vec2

event PlayerDamaged:
    var amount:   int
    var source:   entity_id             # entity_id field in event

event PlayerDied:
    var lives_remaining: int

event EnemyDefeated:
    var position:    vec2
    var enemy_type:  EnemyType
    var score_value: int

event CoinCollected:
    var value: int

event FreezeApplied:
    var duration: float

event SceneTransition:
    var next_state: GameState

# Collision event carries entity_id for trait pattern matching (double dispatch)
event Collision:
    var other:  entity_id               # the other entity involved
    var normal: vec2                    # collision surface normal
    var depth:  float                   # penetration depth

# Marker event — no colon, no fields (body-less form)
event GamePaused

# ── 10. Pure func declarations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rules: no emit, no world access, no recursion.
# Return type follows ')' directly — no arrow token.

func clamp_float(v: float, lo: float, hi: float) float:
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v

func clamp_int(v: int, lo: int, hi: int) int:
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v

func abs_f(v: float) float:
    if v < 0.0:
        return v * -1.0
    return v

func aabb_overlap_x(ax: float, aw: float, bx: float, bw: float) float:
    let half_a  = aw * 0.5
    let half_b  = bw * 0.5
    let dx      = (ax + half_a) - (bx + half_b)
    let overlap = half_a + half_b - abs_f(dx)
    if overlap < 0.0:
        return 0.0
    return overlap

func aabb_overlap_y(ay: float, ah: float, by: float, bh: float) float:
    let half_a  = ah * 0.5
    let half_b  = bh * 0.5
    let dy      = (ay + half_a) - (by + half_b)
    let overlap = half_a + half_b - abs_f(dy)
    if overlap < 0.0:
        return 0.0
    return overlap

# value match expression inside a func — matches on enum type
pub func score_for_enemy(etype: EnemyType, multiplier: int) int:
    var base = 0
    match etype:
        EnemyType.Walker => base = 10
        EnemyType.Flyer  => base = 20
        EnemyType.Boss   => base = 100
    return base * multiplier

# lambda expression: map over list[Item]
func item_prices(items: list[Item]) list[int]:
    return items.map(i => i.price)

# lambda expression with field arithmetic
func inventory_value(items: list[Item]) int:
    return items.reduce(0, acc => acc + 1)

# binary operators: +, -, *, /, %, comparisons, logical and/or/not
func is_in_range(value: float, lo: float, hi: float) bool:
    return value >= lo and value <= hi and not (value == lo and value == hi)

# ── 11. Extern func declarations ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# No body, no colon, no purity/recursion checks.
# Backend provides the implementation (e.g. from cactus_runtime.h).

pub extern func lerp(a: float, b: float, t: float) float
pub extern func sin_f(angle: float) float
pub extern func cos_f(angle: float) float
pub extern func sqrt_f(v: float) float
    extern func get_screen_width() int
    extern func get_screen_height() int
    extern func get_time() float
    extern func draw_rect(pos: vec2, size: vec2, col: color)
    extern func draw_text(text: string, x: float, y: float, size: int, col: color)
pub extern func play_particle_effect(x: float, y: float)
pub extern func get_player_entity() entity_id

# ── 12. Unit declarations ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auto-instantiated at program start (or on module load).
# Bodies now use nested trait blocks directly. Marker traits appear as bare lines.

pub unit Player:
    Position2D:
        pos = vec2(100.0, 300.0)
        velocity = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
    Health:
        health = MAX_HEALTH
        shield = 0
    Inventory:
        gold = 0
        max_slots = 20
    Score:
        score = 0
        high_score = 0
    Renderable2D:
        texture = PlayerTex
        visible = true
        layer = 1
        tint = PLAYER_COLOR
    PlayerOwned

unit Camera2D:
    Camera:
        zoom = 1.0
        active = true
        rotation = 0.0
    FollowCamera
    Persistent

unit AudioManager:
    AudioSettings:
        master_volume = 1.0
        sfx_volume = 0.8
        music_volume = 0.7
    MusicTrack:
        music = ThemeMusic
        playing = true
    Persistent

# Bare config key — valid when field name is unambiguous across applied traits
unit GameManager:
    Score:
        score = 0
        high_score = 0
    Persistent

# ── 13. Template declarations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT auto-instantiated. Spawned via block-structured `spawn TemplateName:`.
# Same nested trait structure as `unit` declarations.

pub template WalkerEnemy:
    Position2D:
        pos = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
        velocity = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
    Health:
        health = 30
    EnemyAI:
        patrol_min_x = 0.0
        patrol_max_x = 400.0
        patrol_speed = 2.0
        enemy_type = EnemyType.Walker
    Renderable2D:
        texture = EnemyTex
        visible = true
        layer = 0
        tint = ENEMY_COLOR

pub template FlyerEnemy:
    Position2D:
        pos = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
        velocity = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
    Health:
        health = 20
    EnemyAI:
        patrol_min_x = 0.0
        patrol_max_x = 600.0
        patrol_speed = 3.5
        enemy_type = EnemyType.Flyer
    Renderable2D:
        texture = EnemyTex
        visible = true
        layer = 0
        tint = ENEMY_COLOR

pub template BossEnemy:
    Position2D:
        pos = vec2(640.0, 200.0)
    Health:
        health = 300
    EnemyAI:
        patrol_speed = 1.0
        enemy_type = EnemyType.Boss
        is_aggro = true
    Boss
    Renderable2D:
        visible = true
        layer = 1
        tint = #FF6600

pub template Coin:
    Position2D:
        pos = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
        velocity = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
    Renderable2D:
        texture = CoinTex
        visible = true
        layer = 0
    Collectible

# ── 14. Systems ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Components of a system declaration:
#   filter:   — trait list; each entry may have "as ALIAS"
#   exclude:  — entities with any of these traits currently attached are skipped
#   order by: — sort entities by field(s) before iteration (section 16)
#   after:    — ordering constraint (run after listed systems in same phase)
#   handlers  — on event_name [as alias]:
#
# EVENT HANDLER SYNTAX:
#   · No parameter list — event data accessed via name: `tick.dt`, `collision.other`
#   · Optional alias:  `on tick as t:` → `t.dt`
#                      `on collision as c:` → `c.other`, `c.normal`
#   · Lifecycle events always in scope from std.core

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# INPUT PHASE — on input:  (no fields on the input event)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system PlayerInputSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos           # filter with alias
        Health as hp
    exclude:
        Frozen                      # frozen entities cannot provide input
        Stunned                     # stunned entities cannot provide input

    on input:
        var jumped   = input.pressed(Jump)       # InputButton → bool
        var fired    = input.down(Fire)          # held down
        var released = input.released(Pause)     # first frame released
        var dx       = input.axis(MoveX)         # InputAxis → float [-1..1]
        var dy       = input.axis(MoveY)
        var dir_vec  = input.axis2(MoveX, MoveY) # two axes → vec2

        pos.velocity = vec2(dx * MOVE_SPEED, dy * MOVE_SPEED)

        if jumped:
            emit PlayerJumped:
                position = pos.pos
                jumps_remaining = 0

        if fired:
            emit PlayerDamaged:
                amount = 1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHYSICS PHASE — on fixed_tick:   access dt as fixed_tick.dt
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system GravitySystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
    exclude:
        Frozen                      # frozen entities skip gravity

    on fixed_tick:
        pos.velocity = vec2(pos.velocity.x, pos.velocity.y + GRAVITY * fixed_tick.dt)
        pos.pos      = pos.pos + vec2(pos.velocity.x * fixed_tick.dt, pos.velocity.y * fixed_tick.dt)

system PhysicsIntegrationSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        EnemyAI as ai
    exclude:
        Frozen
        Stunned                     # stunned enemies don't patrol

    on fixed_tick:
        pos.pos = pos.pos + vec2(ai.patrol_speed * ai.direction * fixed_tick.dt, 0.0)

        if pos.pos.x >= ai.patrol_max_x:
            ai.direction = -1.0
        if pos.pos.x <= ai.patrol_min_x:
            ai.direction = 1.0

system CollisionSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        Health as hp

    after:
        PhysicsIntegrationSystem    # must run after integration in fixed_tick

    on fixed_tick:
        let ox = aabb_overlap_x(pos.pos.x, 32.0, 0.0, 5000.0)
        let oy = aabb_overlap_y(pos.pos.y, 48.0, 600.0, 40.0)

        if ox > 0.0 and oy > 0.0:
            emit PlayerDamaged to get_player_entity():
                amount = 1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UPDATE PHASE — on tick:   access dt as tick.dt  (or alias.dt with `as`)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system HealthSystem:
    filter:
        Health as hp
    exclude:
        Invincible                  # invincible entities skip all damage processing

    on tick as t:
        # `as t` alias — access event fields as t.dt instead of tick.dt
        # Clamp health using pure func call
        hp.health = clamp_int(hp.health, 0, hp.max_health)

    on PlayerDamaged as dmg:
        # User event with alias: access payload as dmg.field
        let damage = dmg.amount                         # let: immutable local binding
        hp.health  = hp.health - damage

        # add with named arg — explicit grace period duration
        add Invincible(duration = 1.5)                  # dynamically attach Invincible trait

        if hp.health <= 0:
            emit PlayerDied:
                lives_remaining = 0

    on spawn:
        # on spawn: fires once after all fields are initialized; no payload fields
        hp.health = hp.max_health

    on destroy:
        # on destroy: fires before entity is removed; fields still readable
        emit EnemyDefeated:
            position = vec2(0.0, 0.0)
            enemy_type = EnemyType.Walker
            score_value = SCORE_PER_COIN

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 15 — DYNAMIC TRAITS: `add` and `remove`
#
# `add`   — attaches a trait (emplace-or-replace; patches if already present)
# `remove` — destroys a trait and its data from an entity
# No `: disabled` / `enable` / `disable` — the old model is replaced entirely.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system FreezeSystem:
    filter:
        Health as hp
        Position2D as pos

    on tick:
        if hp.health < 20:
            add Frozen              # bare add — Frozen is a marker, no fields
        if hp.health > 50:
            remove Frozen           # remove — Frozen detached, entity re-enters gravity/patrol

    on FreezeApplied as fa:
        # Freeze from external event — add both effects
        add Frozen                              # stops movement
        add Invincible(duration = fa.duration)  # named arg: use event field for duration

# Invincibility timer — runs only on entities that currently HAVE Invincible
system InvincibilitySystem:
    filter:
        Invincible as inv           # only entities that were dynamically `add Invincible`d

    on tick:
        inv.duration = inv.duration - tick.dt
        if inv.duration <= 0.0:
            remove Invincible       # timer expired — entity can take damage again

# Stun timer — runs only on entities that currently HAVE Stunned
system StunnedMovementSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        Stunned as stun             # only entities that were `add Stunned`d

    on tick:
        # Slow down stunned entities
        pos.velocity = vec2(
            pos.velocity.x * stun.slow_factor,
            pos.velocity.y * stun.slow_factor
        )
        stun.duration = stun.duration - tick.dt
        if stun.duration <= 0.0:
            remove Stunned          # stun expired — full movement restored

    on fixed_tick:
        # Stunned entities still apply physics at reduced velocity
        pos.pos = pos.pos + vec2(pos.velocity.x * fixed_tick.dt, pos.velocity.y * fixed_tick.dt)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 16 — ENTITY SORT ORDERING: `order by:` on systems
#
# Sorts entities before iteration. Multi-key lexicographic. Per frame.
# Sort keys must be `alias.field` from filter:; must be int/float/bool.
# For vec2 members, use `pos.pos.y` (resolves to float) not `pos.pos` (vec2).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system ScoreSystem:
    filter:
        Score as sc
    exclude:
        Frozen

    on tick:
        sc.score = clamp_int(sc.score, 0, 999999)

    on EnemyDefeated:
        let pts = score_for_enemy(EnemyDefeated.enemy_type, sc.combo_multiplier)
        sc.score = sc.score + pts
        if sc.score > sc.high_score:
            sc.high_score = sc.score

    on CoinCollected:
        sc.score = sc.score + CoinCollected.value * sc.combo_multiplier

system EnemySpawnerSystem:
    filter:
        Score as sc
        Position2D as pos

    on tick:
        # spawn expression — result is entity_id
        let walker_id = spawn WalkerEnemy:
            Position2D:
                pos = vec2(pos.pos.x + 300.0, pos.pos.y)
            EnemyAI:
                patrol_min_x = pos.pos.x + 100.0
                patrol_max_x = pos.pos.x + 500.0

        # cross-entity `add` — freeze the spawned walker for 2 seconds
        add Frozen to walker_id                         # add to another entity

        # spawn statement — discard result
        spawn FlyerEnemy:
            Position2D:
                pos = vec2(pos.pos.x + 500.0, 100.0)

        emit EnemyDefeated:
            position = pos.pos
            enemy_type = EnemyType.Walker
            score_value = SCORE_PER_COIN
        emit PlayerDamaged to walker_id:
            amount = 5

    on EnemyDefeated:
        destroy

system CoinDropSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        EnemyAI as ai

    on EnemyDefeated:
        var coin_id = spawn Coin:
            Position2D:
                pos = EnemyDefeated.position
        emit CoinCollected to coin_id:
            value = SCORE_PER_COIN

system CollectibleSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
    exclude:
        PlayerOwned                 # do not re-collect player-owned entities

    on CoinCollected:
        destroy

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 18 — ENTITY LIVENESS: `exists(entity_id)` built-in
#
# entity_id is an opaque handle. It may become stale after the referenced entity
# is destroyed. `exists()` is a built-in that tests liveness:
#
#   if exists(f.target):         ...   → guard cross-entity access
#   if not exists(f.target):     ...   → clean up dangling refs
#
# All ops on a stale handle are safe no-ops: add/remove, targeted emit, destroy.
# A `match stale_id:` fires NO arms — including `_ =>`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system FollowerSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        Follower as f
    after:
        PhysicsIntegrationSystem

    on tick:
        if exists(f.target):
            # Target is still live — apply follow velocity toward offset
            let spd = f.speed * tick.dt
            pos.velocity = vec2(f.offset.x * spd, f.offset.y * spd)
        if not exists(f.target):
            # Target was destroyed — detach follower cleanly
            # (all ops above on a stale handle would have been safe no-ops anyway)
            remove Follower

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 17 — TRAIT PATTERN MATCHING: `match entity_id:` (double dispatch)
#
# When the subject has type entity_id, `match` dispatches by RUNTIME trait presence:
#   · Arms checked in order — first match wins
#   · `TraitName as alias =>` binds trait data (read/write access)
#   · `TraitName =>` matches marker traits with no data binding
#   · `_ =>` optional wildcard — executes when no arm matched
#   · No wildcard needed — open world, no-match is silent no-op
#
# Under the hood: if (auto* b = registry.try_get<Boss>(c.other)) { ... }
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system CollisionDispatchSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        Health as hp
    exclude:
        Invincible                  # invincible entities bypass all collision damage

    on collision as c:
        # `match c.other:` — c.other is entity_id → TRAIT PATTERN MATCH mode
        match c.other:
            Boss as boss =>
                # Boss collision: heavy damage + self grace period + stun the boss
                hp.health = hp.health - 20
                add Invincible(duration = 2.0)              # self: explicit duration
                add Stunned(duration = 3.0) to c.other      # cross-entity: stun boss

            EnemyAI as enemy =>
                # Enemy collision: damage scales with enemy speed
                hp.health = hp.health - 5
                add Invincible                              # self: uses default (1.5s)
                emit PlayerDamaged:
                    amount = 5

            Collectible =>
                # Collectible collision: no damage — consume the collectible
                emit CoinCollected:
                    value = SCORE_PER_COIN
                remove Collectible from c.other             # cross-entity remove
                destroy c.other

            Frozen =>
                # Frozen obstacle: minor chip damage, no invincibility
                hp.health = hp.health - 1

            _ =>
                # Anything else: environmental contact
                pos.velocity = vec2(pos.velocity.x * -0.5, pos.velocity.y)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POST-UPDATE PHASE — on late_tick:   access dt as late_tick.dt
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SceneRenderSystem — demonstrates `order by:` for render layer + Y-sort
system SceneRenderSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        Renderable2D as rndr
    exclude:
        Frozen
    order by:
        rndr.layer asc              # primary: layer 0 (background) first
        pos.pos.y asc               # secondary: lower Y = further "back" (Y-sort depth)

    on tick:
        if rndr.visible:
            draw_rect(pos.pos, vec2(32.0, 32.0), rndr.tint)

system BossRenderSystem:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        Renderable2D as rndr
        Boss                        # filter on marker trait (no fields accessible)
    order by:
        rndr.layer asc              # boss sprites sorted by layer too

    after:
        SceneRenderSystem           # boss renders on top of normal entities

    on tick:
        if rndr.visible:
            draw_rect(pos.pos, vec2(64.0, 64.0), rndr.tint)

system CameraFollowSystem:
    filter:
        cam_flat.Camera as cam
        cam_flat.FollowCamera as follow

    after:
        PhysicsIntegrationSystem
        CollisionSystem

    on late_tick:
        let smooth = clamp_float(follow.smoothing * late_tick.dt, 0.0, 1.0)
        cam.offset = vec2(
            lerp(cam.offset.x, follow.target_pos.x, smooth),
            lerp(cam.offset.y, follow.target_pos.y, smooth)
        )

system UIRenderSystem:
    filter:
        Score as sc
        Health as hp

    after:
        CameraFollowSystem

    on late_tick:
        let sw = get_screen_width()
        let sh = get_screen_height()

        var bar_w = sw - 20
        bar_w     = clamp_int(bar_w, 0, 1260)

        draw_text(SCORE_LABEL, 10.0, 10.0, 24, PLAYER_COLOR)
        draw_text(LIVES_LABEL, 10.0, 40.0, 24, PLAYER_COLOR)

system DebugOverlaySystem:
    # filter: is optional — no filter means match ALL entities
    after:
        UIRenderSystem
        CameraFollowSystem

    on late_tick:
        let sw = get_screen_width()
        let sh = get_screen_height()
        draw_text(DEBUG_LABEL, 10.0, 70.0, 16, CLEAR_WHITE)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCENE LIFECYCLE — on load:  and on unload:  (no payload fields)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system SceneManager:
    filter:
        Score as sc
        Health as hp

    on load:
        sc.score = 0
        hp.health = MAX_HEALTH

    on unload:
        emit SceneTransition:
            next_state = GameState.Playing

system CleanupSystem:
    exclude:
        std.core.Persistent

    on unload:
        destroy

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GAME FLOW — load + match (value match on enum)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system GameFlowSystem:
    filter:
        Health as hp
        Score as sc

    on tick:
        if hp.health <= 0:
            load game_over

    on SceneTransition as st:
        # `st.next_state` is type GameState (enum) → VALUE match (not trait match)
        match st.next_state:
            GameState.Playing  => load level2
            GameState.GameOver => load game_over
            GameState.MainMenu => load game_over
            GameState.Paused   => emit FreezeApplied:
                duration = 5.0

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PARTICLE SYSTEM — no filter, extern func calls, no trait field access
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

system ParticleSystem:
    after:
        SceneRenderSystem
        BossRenderSystem

    on tick:
        # No filter → no trait field access; only extern calls are valid
        let t = get_time()
        play_particle_effect(
            cos_f(t) * 100.0 + 640.0,
            sin_f(t) * 100.0 + 360.0
        )

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 19 — EXTERN SYSTEM: `extern system` — declarative backend systems
#
# `extern system` declares a filter (and optionally order by:, exclude:, after:)
# but contains NO event handlers. The backend provides the full implementation.
#
# Two patterns:
#   · Stdlib-known:   backend identifies traits by fully-qualified name and
#                     auto-generates a complete rendering / physics / audio pass.
#   · User-defined:   backend generates a typed C++ callback scaffold:
#                     void SystemName_update(registry, entity, TraitA& a, ...)
#
# `extern system` participates in the `after:` ordering graph like any system.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Stdlib-known extern system — backend auto-generates the sprite rendering pass
# because it recognises spr.Renderer + tr_flat.Position as std.render.sprites + std.transform.flat.
# No C++ to write; no parameters to configure; the `order by:` is honoured by the backend.
extern system SpriteRenderPass:
    filter:
        spr.Renderer as r
        tr_flat.Position as pos
    order by:
        r.layer asc
        pos.pos.y asc
    after:
        CollisionSystem

# Stdlib-known extern system — backend auto-generates the 2D physics integration pass
extern system Physics2DPass:
    filter:
        tr_flat.Position as pos
        phys_flat.RigidBody as rb
    after:
        GravitySystem

# User-defined extern system — backend generates a typed C++ callback scaffold.
# The author fills in the implementation in the generated .cpp file:
#   void ParticleEffectRenderer_update(entt::registry& reg,
#                                      entt::entity entity,
#                                      Position2D& pos,
#                                      Visual&     vis);
extern system ParticleEffectRenderer:
    filter:
        Position2D as pos
        Visual as vis
    after:
        SpriteRenderPass
        ParticleSystem
